  "_comment": "Sanitized Revolut /transactions responses, one per pocket uid, shaped after the first real fetch (docs/adr-revolut-onboarding.md decision 8). Structural properties this fixture must preserve: (1) transaction_id is null on every transaction, so FITID falls through to entry_reference; (2) a currency conversion is always two transactions in two different pockets whose entry_reference is one byte-identical 36-char lowercase UUID - here the EUR/USD pair sits entirely inside the shared-master-IBAN group (the data-loss regression case) and the PLN/GBP pair straddles it; (3) the bank_transaction_code vocabulary below (EXCHANGE, TOPUP, TRANSFER) is what one fetch of one connection observed - it is NOT closed, and no test may assert it is; (4) no remittance element is a machine reference (no <PREFIX>-<id> shapes), so Revolut output carries zero CHECKNUM/REFNUM; (5) counterparty presence tracks transaction TYPE, not direction: every non-conversion row carries a party name and account under iban, every conversion leg carries neither. booking_date == value_date (date-only) and exchange_rate is a present-but-null key throughout; instructed_amount is absent entirely.",
